==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|shŭt}}, {{IPA|en|/ʃʌt/}}
* {{IPA|en|/ʃʊt/|a=Northern England}}
* {{i|dialectal|archaic}} {{IPA|en|/ʃɛt/}} {{q|see {{m|en|shet}}}}<ref>{{R:Stanley SET|I|12|27}}</ref>
* {{audio|en|en-us-shut.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ʌt|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*(s)kewd-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|shutten}}, {{m|enm|shetten}}, from {{inh|en|ang|scyttan||to cause rapid movement, shoot a bolt, shut, bolt}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*skutjaną}}, {{m|gem-pro|*skuttijaną||to bar, bolt}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*skuttą}}, {{m|gem-pro|*skuttjō||bar, bolt, shed}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*(s)kewd-||to drive, fall upon, rush}}.

Cognate with {{cog|nl|schutten||to shut in, lock up}}, {{cog|nds|schütten||to shut, lock in}}, {{cog|de|schützen||to shut out, dam, protect, guard}}.

====Verb====
{{en-verb|shuts|shutting|shut|past_ptc2=shutten|past_ptc2_qual=obsolete, dialectal}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[close]], to [[stop]] from being [[open]].
#: {{syn|en|close}}
#: {{ux|en|Please '''shut''' the door.}}
#: {{ux|en|The light was so bright I had to '''shut''' my eyes.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[close]], to [[stop]] being open.
#: {{syn|en|close}}
#: {{ux|en|If you wait too long, the automatic door will '''shut'''.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|or|intransitive|chiefly|British}} To [[close]] (a [[business]] or venue) temporarily or permanently.
#: {{ux|en|They generally '''shut''' the museum each day at 6 pm.}}
#: {{ux|en|The owners were losing money so they've '''shut''' the shop for good.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[confine]] in an enclosed area.
#: {{ux|en|I '''shut''' the cat in the kitchen before going out.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[isolate]], to [[close off]] from the world.
#* {{RQ:Tennyson In Memoriam|XXIII|39|Now, sometimes in my sorrow '''shut''',<br>⁠Or breaking into song by fits;<br>⁠Alone, alone, to where he sits,<br>The Shadow cloak’d from head to foot<br>Who keeps the keys of all the creeds,<br>⁠I wander, often falling lame, {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[catch]] or [[snag]] in the act of shutting something.
#: {{ux|en|He's just gone and '''shut''' his finger in the door!}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[preclude]], [[exclude]].
#: {{syn|en|shut out}}
#* {{RQ:Dryden Virgil|Aeneis
|passage='''shut''' from every shore}}
# {{infl of|en|shut||ed-form}}

=====Usage notes=====
Except when part of one of the derived terms listed below, almost every use of ''shut'' can be replaced by ''[[close]]''. The reverse is not true – there are many uses of ''close'' that cannot be replaced by ''shut''.

