====Adjective====
{{en-adj|-}}

# [[closed|Closed]]; not [[open]], in any of various senses.
## Physically [[sealed]], [[obstructed]], folded together, etc.
##: {{ux|en|A '''shut''' door barred our way into the house.}}
##: {{ux|en|Pleas keep your mouth '''shut''' while you are eating.}}
##: {{ux|en|A book lay '''shut''' on the table.}}
## Not available for use or operation.
##: {{ux|en|Phone lines are now '''shut'''.}}
## {{lb|en|of a business or venue}} Not operating or conducting trade; not allowing [[entrance]] to [[visitors]] or the [[public]].
##: {{ux|en|Banks are '''shut''' on bank holidays.}}
##: {{ux|en|The museum is '''shut''' for the Christmas holidays.}}
## Not [[receptive]].
##: {{ux|en|He mind is '''shut''' to new ideas.}}
# {{lb|en|heraldry}} {{syn of|en|close}}.
# {{lb|en|especially|sports}} Of a [[club]], [[bat]] or other hitting implement, angled [[downwards]] and/or  (for a [[right-hander]]) [[anticlockwise]] of straight.
# {{lb|en|linguistics|phonetics|archaic}} {{synonym of|en|close}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1810|author=Benjamin Humphrey Smart|title=A practical grammar of English pronunciation| page=344| passage=Whenever a syllable is formed with a long, that is an open vowel, they account the syllable long; and whenever formed with a short, that is a '''shut''' vowel, they reckon it short.}}

